# vms-6a1/vms-8146 (SHOW USERS): SHOW USERS + /FULL layout on VAX V7.3. Volatile =
# the title date/time and the 8-hex Process ID in /FULL (2020021A -- its trailing
# nibble can be A-F, so it is masked as a whole 8-hex token before the digit-mask).
# The user/process COUNTS are 1 on a single-user boot (stable, masked to #). Pins:
# the "OpenVMS User Processes at" banner, the "Total number of users / processes"
# line, and BOTH column headers (default: Username/Node/Interactive/Subprocess/
# Batch; /FULL: Username/Node/Process Name/PID/Terminal) + the SYSTEM row shape.
ARCH=vax
DESC="SHOW USERS + /FULL banner, counts line, and both column headers (date/PID/counts masked)"
NORMALIZE='s/[0-9A-F]\{8\}/########/g; s/[0-9]/#/g'
COMMANDS=(
  'SHOW USERS'
  'SHOW USERS/FULL'
)
# MACHINE_MASK (rd vms-6a1): the values that legitimately vary by product,
# machine and moment -- masked so the gate compares the labelled STRUCTURE:
#   1. the banner's PRODUCT word: VMS prints "OpenVMS User Processes at", OVMX
#      its own name (INV-0: OVMX never claims the OpenVMS mark as its identity,
#      the same reason SHOW SYSTEM's banner differs). One capitalised word is
#      required, so a missing banner word still reds;
#   2. the MONTH of the banner date (NORMALIZE masks only its digits);
#   3. the NODE column of the SYSTEM row -- VAX "VAX1" vs OVMX's own SCSNODE.
#      The username and the count/PID/terminal columns stay compared.
MACHINE_MASK='s/^( +)[A-Z][A-Za-z]+ (User Processes at )/\1<PRODUCT> \2/; s/(User Processes at +#+)-[A-Z]{3}-/\1-<MON>-/; s/^( SYSTEM +)[A-Z][A-Z0-9#]*( )/\1<NODE>\2/'
